WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.275 --> 00:00:04.950
This commit fixes three player bugs: clipped code, a pointer that misses

2
00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:08.200
its words, and a play button drawn over the wrong slide.

3
00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:11.225
We'll walk the real diff, then cover what to watch.

4
00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:16.500
Before this commit, long code lines were clipped instead of shrunk.

5
00:00:16.475 --> 00:00:19.400
The pointer drifted off the words it pointed at.

6
00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:22.550
And the play button sat over the title area even when you

7
00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:24.150
resumed mid-walkthrough.

8
00:00:25.125 --> 00:00:28.250
The old code reset and applied CSS zoom.

9
00:00:28.225 --> 00:00:32.450
Under zoom, text-range bounding boxes come back in the wrong coordinate space,

10
00:00:32.375 --> 00:00:33.900
so the pointer missed.

11
00:00:33.875 --> 00:00:37.988
The new code [clears the transform](# "transform = """), then measures the natural size, taking

12
00:00:37.838 --> 00:00:40.300
the larger of offset and scroll width.

13
00:00:40.275 --> 00:00:44.813
It computes a scale, snaps near-one values to exactly one, clamps at

14
00:00:44.663 --> 00:00:47.900
zero point three, and applies it as a transform.

15
00:00:47.887 --> 00:00:51.100
The scale is also stored on the element so the measure script

16
00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:51.925
can read it.

17
00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:56.850
A transform doesn't change layout, so the content must keep its natural

18
00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:57.675
size.

19
00:00:57.675 --> 00:01:01.775
Flex none stops the flexbox squeezing it, and max width none lets

20
00:01:01.625 --> 00:01:05.025
a long code line run wide so it gets measured and shrunk

21
00:01:04.875 --> 00:01:06.300
instead of clipped.

22
00:01:06.338 --> 00:01:09.725
Scaling from the centre keeps it centred in the slide body.

23
00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:13.950
Diagrams and images still flex, because they size themselves.

24
00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:18.575
Each slide eases in from a few pixels below, so a pointer

25
00:01:18.425 --> 00:01:20.650
measured at once is slightly off.

26
00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:24.712
Now, on animation end, if this slide is still current, the cue

27
00:01:24.562 --> 00:01:27.400
key is cleared and the pointer re-measured.

28
00:01:27.412 --> 00:01:31.175
In the overlay, at title checks the current segment, so the button

29
00:01:31.025 --> 00:01:34.450
only sits over the title when the title slide is showing.

30
00:01:35.425 --> 00:01:39.250
The new test file starts a daemon with fake speech, builds one

31
00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:43.450
walkthrough with every slide kind, and runs it in landscape, square and

32
00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:44.500
portrait.

33
00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:47.488
For each slide it seeks to just after a cue, takes a

34
00:01:47.338 --> 00:01:52.250
screenshot into a git-ignored folder, then asserts the slide kind, no render

35
00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:56.338
errors, the visual inside the stage, and the pointer within twenty pixels

36
00:01:56.188 --> 00:01:56.875
of it.

37
00:01:57.900 --> 00:01:59.400
Five things to watch.

38
00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:03.137
First: a transform leaves the layout box at full size, so a

39
00:02:02.987 --> 00:02:07.063
wide box still overflows the slide body; it's hidden today only because

40
00:02:06.913 --> 00:02:08.950
the slide has overflow hidden.

41
00:02:08.975 --> 00:02:12.725
Second: the floor dropped from zero point three five to zero point

42
00:02:12.575 --> 00:02:15.175
three, and anything needing less still clips.

43
00:02:15.175 --> 00:02:19.713
Third: animation end bubbles, so a child animation added later would trigger

44
00:02:19.563 --> 00:02:23.050
the re-measure early; checking the event target would harden it.

45
00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:26.625
With reduced motion there is no animation, which is fine.

46
00:02:27.025 --> 00:02:30.900
Fourth: the test's variable is called first but takes the last cue;

47
00:02:30.912 --> 00:02:32.800
harmless, but misleading.

48
00:02:32.837 --> 00:02:38.262
Fifth: the browser tests skip unless Playwright's Chromium is installed, so CI

49
00:02:38.112 --> 00:02:39.750
won't run them by default.
